[{"id":5165229302,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDUxNjUyMjkzMDI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/events/5165229302","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2021-08-16T20:20:02Z","label":{"name":"requires triage","color":"ffff00"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/899798938","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/6889#issuecomment-899798938","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/6889","id":899798938,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB841odea","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-08-16T20:30:25Z","updated_at":"2021-08-16T20:30:25Z","body":"the most expensive coercion is the \"binary\" coercion we do when we create a WHERE clause; for a lazy loader, we aren't doing this coercion in any case.\r\n\r\nin the perf suite, I get the same performance from both of these runs, this is not even trying to be very optimized:\r\n\r\n```py\r\n@Profiler.profile\r\ndef test_orm_query_new_style_using_external_lambdas(n):\r\n    \"\"\"new style ORM select() of the full entity w/ external lambdas.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    session = Session(bind=engine)\r\n    for id_ in random.sample(ids, n):\r\n\r\n        stmt = lambdas.lambda_stmt(lambda: future_select(Customer))\r\n        stmt += lambda s: s.where(Customer.id == id_)\r\n        session.execute(stmt).scalar_one()\r\n\r\n@Profiler.profile\r\ndef test_orm_query_new_style_using_raw_construction(n):\r\n    \"\"\"new style ORM select() of the full entity w/ raw construction\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    session = Session(bind=engine)\r\n    for id_ in random.sample(ids, n):\r\n\r\n        stmt = select(Customer)\r\n        stmt = stmt.where(lambda: Customer.id == id_)\r\n        session.execute(stmt).scalar_one()\r\n```\r\n\r\nthat is, the ``Customer.id == id_`` seems to be the big difference between them, so if i keep that as a lambda, the times are 1.72 sec vs. 1.86 sec, negligble.   lazy loader already has the criteria built up.\r\n\r\nif I do totally raw Select in a more inlined way, this runs in 1.6 sec.   no lambdas needed, which will be helpful to simplify how the ORM does things:\r\n\r\n```py\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.sql.expression import Select\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import inspect\r\n\r\n@Profiler.profile\r\ndef test_orm_query_new_style_using_raw_construction(n):\r\n    \"\"\"new style ORM select() of the full entity w/ raw construction\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    table = inspect(Customer).__clause_element__()\r\n\r\n    crit = Customer.id == 10\r\n    session = Session(bind=engine)\r\n    for id_ in random.sample(ids, n):\r\n\r\n        stmt = Select.__new__(Select)\r\n        stmt.__dict__.update(\r\n            _raw_columns=[table],\r\n            _propagate_attrs=table._propagate_attrs,\r\n            _label_style=LABEL_STYLE_DISAMBIGUATE_ONLY,\r\n            _where_criteria=(crit, )\r\n        )\r\n        session.execute(stmt).scalar_one()\r\n```\r\n\r\nif we perhaps add some helper constructors to Select and keep them underscored, we can basically just inline the production of Select for the few places we are doing it now and it won't be impossible to debug / expand upon.     right now in https://gerrit.sqlalchemy.org/c/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/+/3001 im looking at such complexity that using `stmt.compile()` will not give you the correct parameters without taking external parameters into account, which was intended to be something that would only be needed if caching were turned on.   but because the \"stale\" parameters are still stuck in the lambda callables, there's this whole second level of caching that I can barely keep my head around.    I'd like this code to be maintainable by others.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/899798938/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"